gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 115, lesson_id: 30, number: 1, title: "USE OF 'AG' 'BY, AS A RESULT OF'", position: 1, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.046851Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.049467Z")
gr.body = "<!-- BEGIN app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><div class=\"lexxy-content\">\n  <!-- BEGIN /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><p>Ag can be used with adjectives to express the idea 'as a result of someone's action, or of some active force'. It can also be used with a passive construction of the sort tá an teach dhá thógáil 'the house is being built' (see Lesson 15) to indicate the agent.</p>\n<!-- END /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb --></div>\n<!-- END app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb -->"; gr.save!
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 116, lesson_id: 30, number: 2, title: "GENITIVE WITH SLENDER CONSONANT AND -E (CTD.)", position: 2, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.058757Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.058757Z")
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 117, lesson_id: 30, number: 3, title: "USE OF ADJECTIVE WITH GENITIVE OF FEMININE NOUNS", position: 3, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.071459Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.071459Z")
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 118, lesson_id: 30, number: 4, title: "MORE ADJECTIVES WITH SPECIAL COMPARATIVE FORM", position: 4, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.077473Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:49:49.077473Z")
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 119, lesson_id: 31, number: 1, title: "PAST/CONDITIONAL OF COPULA", position: 1, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.783190Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.788825Z")
gr.body = "<!-- BEGIN app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><div class=\"lexxy-content\">\n  <!-- BEGIN /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><p>Ba chuma le Cáit faoin mbainne. Cáit didn't/wouldn't mind about the milk. The copula has only a present (is, ní, ar, etc., see Lesson 11) and a past or conditional. The forms of the past and conditional are the same.</p>\n<!-- END /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb --></div>\n<!-- END app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb -->"; gr.save!
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 120, lesson_id: 31, number: 2, title: "RELATIVE OF PAST/CONDITIONAL OF COPULA", position: 2, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.801116Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.801116Z")
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 121, lesson_id: 31, number: 3, title: "PAST/CONDITIONAL OF COPULA WITH FHEARR ETC.", position: 3, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.812806Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.812806Z")
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 122, lesson_id: 31, number: 4, title: "GENITIVE WITH BROAD CONSONANT", position: 4, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.822574Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:50:30.825242Z")
gr.body = "<!-- BEGIN app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><div class=\"lexxy-content\">\n  <!-- BEGIN /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><p>abhainn river bruach na habhann the bank of the river</p><p>athair /æ:/ father teach m'athar /a:/ my father's house</p><p>There are a limited number of nouns (all feminine except athair) which form the genitive by making the final consonant broad, e.g. abhainn 'river', bruach na habhann 'of the river'.</p><p>Similar to abhainn are: tórainn 'border', claí na tórann 'boundary wall'; Árainn 'Aran', muintir Árann 'the people of Aran'; artachain 'misfortune', in aghaidh na hanachain 'against misfortune'; Albain 'Scotland', muintir na hAlban 'the people of Scotland'; Nollaig 'Christmas', aimsir na Nollag 'Christmastime'; máthair 'mother', teach mo mháthar 'my mother's house'.</p><p>All these forms are pronounced according to the tables in Appendix I. Where the vowel changes it is shown above.</p>\n<!-- END /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb --></div>\n<!-- END app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb -->"; gr.save!
gr = GrammarRule.create!(id: 123, lesson_id: 34, number: 1, title: "EMPHATIC WORD ORDER", position: 1, created_at: "2026-04-11T22:53:20.481463Z", updated_at: "2026-04-11T22:53:20.486915Z")
gr.body = "<!-- BEGIN app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><div class=\"lexxy-content\">\n  <!-- BEGIN /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb\n--><p>The copula (see Lesson 11) can be used to emphasise or 'front' the part of a sentence to which particular importance is given.</p>\n<!-- END /Users/seosamh/.rbenv/versions/ruby-3.4.2/lib/ruby/gems/3.4.0/gems/actiontext-8.1.3/app/views/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb --></div>\n<!-- END app/views/layouts/action_text/contents/_content.html.erb -->"; gr.save!
